    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01HGK75K0MPZPTKB3KQT5XD1VP\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to remove Klaviyo onsite tracking from your Shopify store, which includes both <em>Active on Site</em> and <em>Viewed Product</em> tracking, and may also include <em>Viewed Collection</em>, <em>Submitted Search</em>, and <em>Added to Cart</em> tracking depending on your setup. For more context, read <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/4425956184731\">our article about onsite tracking for Shopify</a>. </p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HGK75K0N0FBCRS6PTW0DS4FQ\">Before you begin</h2>\n<p>You may wish to remove onsite tracking for site speed performance reasons, though Klaviyo.js has recently been updated to <a href=\"https://klaviyo.tech/improving-forms-performance-c67c98114d49\">minimize its impact</a> in this regard. Note that Klaviyo’s Shopify app embed bypasses the website’s native tag manager and can result in faster loading of Klaviyo’s JavaScript. Additionally, we track some events via a Shopify Server Pixel (<em>Viewed Collection</em>, <em>Submitted Search</em>, and <em>Added to Cart</em>).</p>\n<p>You can: </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove <em>Viewed Product</em> tracking</li>\n<li>Remove <em>Viewed Collection</em>, <em>Submitted Search</em>, and <em>Added to Cart </em>tracking</li>\n<li>Remove all onsite tracking</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The first means you will not be able to track when someone views a product on your store, meaning you will not be able to send browse abandonment messages. </p>\n<p>If you remove all onsite tracking, you will also no longer be able to use Klaviyo sign-up forms. </p>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>The guidance below around removing <em>Added to Cart</em> tracking refers to the Shopify-branded <em>Added to Cart</em> event synced via Shopify Server Pixel. If you wish to remove <em>Added to Cart</em> tracking that you enabled via a code snippet, check out <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/28709780787355\">our guide</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HGK75K0NHHED15T7H26KWN54\">Remove Viewed Product tracking</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>In Klaviyo, select the <strong>Integrations </strong>tab.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Shopify.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Uncheck the <em>Track 'Viewed Product' events </em>setting.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28709107573275\" alt=\"\" width=\"479\" height=\"255\">\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Update Settings</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01J6F9PPGPMZDPWV64VSAP7SBK\">Remove Viewed Collection, Submitted Search, and Added to Cart</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>In Klaviyo, select the <strong>Integrations </strong>tab.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Shopify.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Uncheck the <em>Track behavioral events </em>setting.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28709113412123\" alt=\"\" width=\"484\" height=\"258\">\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Update Settings</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HGK75K0N32TF1GJVSPWA5MGA\">Remove all onsite tracking</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>In Klaviyo, select the <strong>Integrations </strong>tab.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Shopify.</strong>\n</li>\n<li>Uncheck the <em>Track 'Viewed Product' events</em> and <em>Track behavioral events </em>settings.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28709113412123\" alt=\"\" width=\"484\" height=\"258\">\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Update Settings</strong>.</li>\n<li>Click<strong> Edit</strong> next to <em>The Klaviyo app embed is enabled on your Shopify store </em>to be brought to Shopify.</li>\n<li>Log in if prompted.</li>\n<li>Toggle off the app embed. <br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28710075007131\" alt=\"\" width=\"225\" height=\"287\">\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HGK75K0NS04DWMXPG4YNYWBN\">Outcome</h2>\n<p>You have now removed selected onsite tracking from your Shopify store.</p>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
